{"id":56726,"ord":86,"n_segments":179,"prev":56725,"next":56727,"doc":{"id":"68154","title":"68154_Gus Johnson oral history interview","collection":"rutgers","inst":"Rutgers — Institute of Jazz Studies","interviewee":"Gus Johnson","interviewer":"","date":"","year":"","source_url":"https://rucore.libraries.rutgers.edu/rutgers-lib/68154/","url":"https://semlab.io/linked-jazz-transcripts/?t=68154"},"chapter":"Jay McShann's band","title":"Rooming with Jay and the jam sessions","category":"band_or_employer","summary":"Gus and Jay roomed together on Park Avenue and held rehearsals and jam sessions with the other players.","period":"1938-39","year_from":1938,"year_to":1938,"words":194,"start":[180,13],"end":[182,8],"url":"https://semlab.io/linked-jazz-transcripts/?t=68154#s56726","tags":{"places":[{"name":"Kansas City","focus":1,"type":"city"},{"name":"Park Avenue","focus":0,"type":"street","in":"Kansas City"}],"venues":[],"bands":[{"name":"Jay McShann Orchestra","focus":0,"leader":"Jay McShann"}]},"people":[{"name":"Jay McShann","qid":"Q1684347","n":2},{"name":"Earl Jackson","qid":null,"n":1}],"story":{"theme":17,"theme_name":"Playing with Count Basie: joining, leading, leaving","community":30,"community_name":"Playing with Count Basie: the band, its feel and its people","core":false},"blocks":[{"p":180,"b":13,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"That's right. We used to have little sessions at the house where we stayed in Kansas City."},{"p":180,"b":14,"s":"MS.","x":"Whose house?"},{"p":181,"b":0,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"Where Jay and I stayed."},{"p":181,"b":1,"s":"MS.","x":"Oh, you and Jay stayed in the same --"},{"p":181,"b":2,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"We were rooming --"},{"p":181,"b":3,"s":"MS.","x":"Oh, you were? Rooming together?"},{"p":181,"b":4,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"Yes, yes, we roomed together."},{"p":181,"b":5,"s":"MS.","x":"For heaven's sake."},{"p":181,"b":6,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"Yes, that was on Park Street, Park Avenue, in Kansas City."},{"p":181,"b":7,"s":"MS.","x":"Yeah."},{"p":181,"b":8,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"And we'd have jam sessions between the fellows, all the fellows would come over to rehearse. Then we'd have the jam sessions."},{"p":181,"b":9,"s":"MS.","x":"No kidding. And then would you be out on the street a lot, at night, to see everybody and everything?"},{"p":181,"b":10,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"Oh, sure. That was all the time. Sure, that was it."},{"p":181,"b":11,"s":"MS.","x":"Was anybody drinking heavy or --"},{"p":181,"b":12,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"What, in our group?"},{"p":181,"b":13,"s":"MS.","x":"Yeah. Mostly --"},{"p":181,"b":14,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"No, not drinking heavy."},{"p":181,"b":15,"s":"MS.","x":"Just enjoying yourselves."},{"p":181,"b":16,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"We were just enjoying ourselves. One of those things."},{"p":181,"b":17,"s":"MS.","x":"Yeah."},{"p":181,"b":18,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"Earl Jackson, he would get pretty"},{"p":182,"b":0,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"juiced at times, but not enough to mess up."},{"p":182,"b":1,"s":"MS.","x":"No."},{"p":182,"b":2,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"See."},{"p":182,"b":3,"s":"MS.","x":"Everybody was wrapped up in the music."},{"p":182,"b":4,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"Right, that's right."},{"p":182,"b":5,"s":"MS.","x":"Yeah."},{"p":182,"b":6,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"If we did get kind of juiced, nobody knew it, nobody but --"},{"p":182,"b":7,"s":"MS.","x":"But yourself."},{"p":182,"b":8,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"-- the guys in the band."}]}